# Rules for the "entailed" matching level of triple evaluation.
#
# Each line says how two predicates, classes or entities relate. The scorer
# closes these rules together with the harness schema and the DBLP seed schema
# (OWL 2 RL, owlrl) and then credits a run triple when it logically implies a
# gold triple (recall) or is implied by one (precision).
#
#   rdfs:subPropertyOf      A is a narrower kind of B        (A implies B, not the reverse)
#   owl:equivalentProperty  A and B are two names for one relation
#   owl:inverseOf           A is B read in the other direction
#   rdfs:subClassOf         every A is a B (for rdf:type triples)
#   owl:sameAs              two names for the same entity
#
# Invented predicates use the hrn: namespace with the exact spelling the
# harness emits (case-sensitive), e.g. hrn:hasAttackTask for "hasAttackTask".
# Add a rule only when it holds in every context; anything weaker belongs to
# the soft level (variants or the judge). Record why in a comment.
# Known limit: owl:sameAs between two author names does not yet reach the
# objects of dblp:authoredBy (those are keyed as person slugs).
# Background and examples: labelling/docs/EVALUATION.md, "Entailed level".

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix dblp: <https://dblp.org/rdf/schema#> .
@prefix hrn:  <https://harness.local/schema#> .

# The harness predicates title/authoredBy/year/venue/cites are already linked to
# DBLP by the harness schema, and the DBLP seed brings its own hierarchy
# (dblp:authoredBy is a kind of dblp:createdBy, inverse of dblp:authorOf).
# No invented-predicate rules are active yet: add them as invented predicates
# appear in reviewed gold.
# The CS-KG content core (harness_semantic, HARNESS_CONTENT_CORE=cskg) is part of
# the harness schema: addresses, evaluatesOn (a kind of usesDataset), the relations
# declared equivalent to CS-KG (hrn:uses = cskg-ont:uses, ...) and CS-KG's inverses
# (cskg-ont:usedBy) are closed without rules here.

# Examples (from the nlp27 worked example); enable only after checking they hold:
# hrn:hasAttackTask   rdfs:subPropertyOf     hrn:evaluatesAttack .
# hrn:addresses       owl:equivalentProperty hrn:addressesProblem .
# hrn:authorOf        owl:inverseOf          dblp:authoredBy .
# hrn:HybridRAGMethod rdfs:subClassOf        hrn:Method .
